            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-69152",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via unbounded intermediate arrays"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The brace-expansion library generates arbitrary strings containing a common prefix and suffix. Prior to 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, and 5.0.9, expand() does not apply maxLength while constructing comma-alternative intermediate arrays or padded sequences, allowing attacker-controlled input to exhaust memory or block the event loop. The fix for CVE-2026-14257 is bypassed by the vulnerability. This issue is fixed in versions 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, and 5.0.9."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-69152",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-69152\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: brace-expansion\nFixed Version: 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, 5.0.9\nLink: [CVE-2026-69152](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-69152)\nThe brace-expansion library generates arbitrary strings containing a common prefix and suffix. Prior to 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, and 5.0.9, expand() does not apply maxLength while constructing comma-alternative intermediate arrays or padded sequences, allowing attacker-controlled input to exhaust memory or block the event loop. The fix for CVE-2026-14257 is bypassed by the vulnerability. This issue is fixed in versions 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, and 5.0.9.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-69152**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|brace-expansion|1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, 5.0.9|[CVE-2026-69152](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-69152)|\n\nThe brace-expansion library generates arbitrary strings containing a common prefix and suffix. Prior to 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, and 5.0.9, expand() does not apply maxLength while constructing comma-alternative intermediate arrays or padded sequences, allowing attacker-controlled input to exhaust memory or block the event loop. The fix for CVE-2026-14257 is bypassed by the vulnerability. This issue is fixed in versions 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, and 5.0.9."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
